  "final_message": "The yen receipt test passes now, and the full suite is green (18/18).\n\n**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` always divided by 100 and added two decimals. Yen has no minor unit, so `500` (already ¥500) was printed as `¥5.00`.\n\n**Fix:** I added a `ZERO_DECIMAL` set containing `JPY`. For those currencies, `formatMoney` prints the amount as whole units with no decimals. GBP, USD and EUR keep two decimals. The helper is shared with the invoice, cart and receipt code, so those now format yen correctly too.\n\nSpot checks: `formatMoney(500, 'JPY')` gives `¥500`, `formatMoney(1250, 'GBP')` gives `£12.50`.\n\nI haven't committed the change. The only modified file is `src/utils/money.js`. I also didn't read `docs/payments.md` because the rate limit blocked it, so the fix follows the code and test rather than the docs.",
